  "master_resume_text": "ROCHELLE MAGPANTAY\nPARTNERSHIPS, GROWTH & IMPLEMENTATION LEADER\nChange Adoption | Cross-Functional Enablement | Practical AI Fluency\n\nEXECUTIVE PROFILE\nI am an experienced partnerships, growth, and implementation leader who understands how to earn trust, translate complexity, and help people adopt new ways of working. I am now adding practical AI fluency so I can help customers and organizations use emerging technology in ways that improve real business outcomes. Across 20+ years, I have pioneered and scaled a fully virtual operating model, launched a new customer vertical, led distributed training and coaching, and managed complex enterprise relationships across multiple markets.\n\nCORE STRENGTHS\nStrategic Partnerships, Growth & Market Development, Program & Implementation Leadership, Go-to-Market Strategy, Change Leadership & Adoption, Cross-Functional Alignment, Workflow Design & Documentation, Training, Workshops & Playbooks, Operating-Model Design, Adoption & Performance Measurement, Executive Communication, Practical AI Fluency, Process Improvement, Early Adoption Sales Process & Implementation\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nSelected to help create and implement a 100% virtual sales operating model, transforming a territory-based, in-home process into repeatable virtual practices for recruiting, onboarding, coaching, communication, and performance management. Helped define the steps, procedures, and controls required for nationwide implementation while maintaining compliance with state and federal insurance regulations. Validated the approach through a successful 90-day pilot, then helped translate the model into easily implementable steps for both new and veteran sales agents to adopt in the field, expanding nationwide remote sales and contributing to 375% company growth during COVID. Created the company's first Veterans Division, identified an underserved market opportunity, built VFW and AMVETS relationships, and proved the vertical over two years; its success helped influence a companywide market-specialization strategy. Recruited, coached, and enabled distributed sales agents; delivered recurring Master Trainings, shared best practices with leadership, and turned frontline feedback into clearer guidance and more consistent execution.\n\nManaged 5,000+ accounts across three states, coordinating negotiation, implementation, operations, collections, retention, and ongoing relationship management while opening new territories and supporting mergers. Used customer, market, and competitive insight to prioritize growth opportunities, adapt plans across diverse markets, and communicate clear recommendations to internal partners and client decision-makers. Exceeded new-sales quota four consecutive years while winning and retaining enterprise relationships including Nike, IKEA, Intel, Daimler, Topgolf, and Dave's Killer Bread.\n\nSelected by management to train new hires because of an ability to make customer discovery, objection handling, and the end-to-end sales process practical, understandable, and human. Delivered executive presentations and built a repeatable business-development model that supported consistent growth through partnerships, referrals, industry organizations, and trusted customer relationships. Led 25+ sales professionals and three operations team members, including hiring, weekly development sessions, coaching, customer experience, performance management, and store profitability. Consulted with executives and owners of 1-99 employee businesses, translating operational needs into practical technology solutions and coordinating implementation and post-sale support. Proposed a Simplifying the Business process improvement projected to save approximately $40,000 per month.\n\nEDUCATION & PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT\nB.S., Multimedia & Web Design. AI Professional Development in progress: Google AI Professional Certificate; Anthropic coursework in AI Fluency: Framework & Foundations, Claude 101, Claude Platform 101, Claude Cowork, Agent Skills, Claude Code, API fundamentals, MCP concepts, and AI Fluency for Small Businesses. Actively applying this coursework using ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini for business research, workflow design, and structured planning. Additional development: team leadership, project management, relationship building, consultative selling, advanced leadership and management, iPEC coaching training. Certified in Psychology of Selling."
